{{also|harn}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|-}} and {{inh|de|goh|harn}}, from the {{der|de|ine-pro|-}} root {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ḱer-||dung, filth}}. Cognate with {{cog|lt|šarmas|t=lye}} (for semantic connection, compare {{m|en|lant}}). Exclusively [[High German]] form without [[s-mobile]] alongside {{cog|gem-pro|*skarną|t=dung}}, whence dialectal {{cog|en|sharn}} and {{m+|de|Schierling|t=[[hemlock]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/harn/|[haʁn]|[haɐ̯n]|[haːn]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Harn.ogg}}
* {{homophones|de|Hahn|qq1=some speakers|Haaren|harren|qq3=casual speech}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m,s:es}}

# {{lb|de|elevated|rare}} [[urine]]
#: {{syn|de|q1=usual formal word|Urin|q2=familiar|Pipi|q3=coarse|Pisse}}

====Usage notes====
* Now used chiefly in several medical compounds. Otherwise it is highly formal and rare.
* Outside of a scientific-medical context, ''Harn'' is more often used for animals than humans.

